Patch to test/mosq_test.py of Eclipse Mosquitto (github.com/eclipse-mosquitto/mosquitto,
commit fda14f2c196d9d2fcdd07d6c5d31a673524f7368), applied by setup.sh.
Mosquitto is dual licensed EPL-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause (Eclipse Distribution License 1.0);
this modification is offered under the same terms.

What it changes (only the comparison of what the broker sends; no test changes):
- expect_packet() reads whole MQTT packets (fixed header + remaining length) instead
  of len(expected) bytes, so a packet of another allowed length does not eat the next.
- packet_matches() accepts the encodings the spec allows for the same content:
  MQTT 5 properties in any order (MQTT-2.2.2), and the Reason Code / Property Length
  a sender may omit (PUBACK..PUBCOMP, DISCONNECT, AUTH). It prints STANDIN-NOTE.
- STANDIN_SUBACK_REORDER=1: what-if pass that keeps a PUBLISH received before the
  SUBACK for the next expect_packet() (MQTT-3.8.4 lets a server send it first).

